  "answer_core": "I wouldn’t try to settle everything at once. Break this into smaller, reversible steps: get legal or professional guidance, decide how you want to handle blocking and phone access, plan what to share with your ex, and set up therapy and a path back to honesty with your daughter. A professional (RAINN, a therapist, or counsel) can help you judge whether reporting or sharply cutting contact is needed, because those steps can improve safety but can also push the contact into less visible places.\n\nSilence on his side is weak evidence. Keep clear tripwires: any request to meet, sexual images, threats, pressure for secrecy, new accounts, contact after a clear stop, or signs he’s talking to other minors. If any appear, update the plan quickly.\n\nWith your ex, share enough context to prevent minimization, but avoid forwarding screenshots or exact wording that could be repeated back to your daughter. Aim for safety and a path back to honest communication, not punishment for its own sake.",
